- W | set a date, tell everyone, and hold yourself to it | v: conformity, achievement | self_control: + | chance: 62
- B | take the first small risk this month, and let the plan catch up | v: achievement, power | chance: 62
- R | start tomorrow, badly, and learn as you go | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 66
- G | ask whether the plan still fits the life you have, and let it go if not | v: security, tradition | chance: 66
- W>G | promise {friend} the two of you will build the first piece together this spring | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 58
- U>W | give the plan to a club that can use it, so the work is not wasted | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 52
- B>U | sell a share of the idea to someone who will push you to finish it | v: power, achievement | chance: 58
- R>B | give up the evening job and put every free hour into it, for yourself at last | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 62
- G>R | start with the part you enjoy most, outdoors, with your own hands | v: hedonism, tradition | chance: 62
works: The first piece is built by the summer, rougher than planned and better for it.
works: Letting it go brings a lightness {N} had not expected.
fails: Another winter goes by, and the plan goes back in the drawer with new figures.
fails: The start is rushed, the first try fails, and the plan seems further away than ever.

