- W | ask the family what would be best for everyone, and go along with it | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 62
- B | pick the place that keeps your money and your independence, and book a viewing | v: self-direction, security | chance: 62
- R | ring the first place in the folder, and say yes on the phone | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 66
- G | stay put, and change the house instead: a bed downstairs, a rail on the wall | v: tradition, security | mark: stayed home | chance: 66
- W>U | promise {friend} a decision by the end of the month, and keep the promise | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 58
- U>B | pay an adviser to choose, and take their answer | v: security, achievement | chance: 52
- B>R | sell the house and spend the difference on living well | v: hedonism, power | chance: 58
- R>G | move in with the friend down the road, and argue happily about the garden | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 62
- G>W | move to where your oldest friends already live, and take your place among them | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: moved away | chance: 62
works: The move is made by spring, and {N} wonders why it took three winters.
works: The house is changed around {N}, and the stairs stop ruling the day.
fails: A fall on the stairs makes the decision for {N}, in a hospital corridor.
fails: Another winter passes with the folder on the table, and the choice gets harder.

