- G | let the work speak for the group, and the group for itself | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 66
- W>R | insist the whole group comes to the meeting, and make it a party afterwards | v: universalism, hedonism | chance: 62
- U>G | write the group's method up so the others can build on it | v: universalism, benevolence | chance: 58
- B>W | take the meeting, then use it to get {friend} a place on the next project | v: power, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 52
- R>U | tell {boss} the two of you want the harder project next, and grab it together | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 58
- G>B | stay quiet now, and trust that people who share credit go further over the years | v: tradition, achievement | chance: 62
works: {friend} hears what {N} said in the room, and does not forget it.
works: The meeting goes well, and the group stays a group.
fails: {friend} finds out from someone else, and the friendship goes cold.
fails: The credit sticks for a month, and then the whispers start.

