- U>B | hire a coach to teach you how other people keep their friends | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 58
- B>R | buy the best tickets in town, and take {friend}, whom you have not seen in years | v: hedonism, power | chance: 52
- R>G | turn up at {friend}'s door unannounced, with a cake and no excuse | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 58
- G>W | go back to the town you grew up in for a weekend, and look people up | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: came home | chance: 62
works: One call leads to another, and by winter there are people to ring.
works: {friend} opens the door, laughs, and lets {N} in.
fails: The calls go unanswered, and {N} goes back to work.
fails: The party is well catered and half empty.

