life: work, conscience
horizon: days
roles: boss, colleague
earth: {boss} tore into {N} in front of everyone, and {N} wants to say exactly what {N} thinks
scene: {boss} tore into {Ns} work in front of the whole team, and half of it was unfair. {N} is on {Ns} feet, face hot, with every word already in place.
scene R: {N} has swallowed it for two years. Today {N} could say all of it, out loud, and walk out free.
- R | say all of it, in front of everyone, and slam the door | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: defied an authority | chance: 40
- W | sit down, and raise it through the proper complaint in the morning | v: conformity, security | chance: 66
- U | ask for a meeting, bring the facts, and show where the criticism was wrong | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 66
- B | smile, and start looking for a better job with a better title | v: achievement, power | chance: 62
- G | let it pass today, and talk it out with {colleague} on the walk home | v: benevolence, security | chance: 62
- W>U | ask the union rep to sit in on a meeting, and learn exactly where you stand | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 62
- U>B | write it all down, calmly, and keep it for when it counts | v: security, power | chance: 62
- B>R | negotiate your way out with a good reference, and go and do what you love | v: power, self-direction | chance: 58
- R>G | stand up for {colleague}, who got it worse, and walk out together | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 52
- G>W | wait for the right moment, and say your piece once, quietly, where it counts | v: security, universalism | chance: 58
works: The air clears, and {boss} is careful with {N} from then on.
works: {N} leaves on {Ns} own terms, with a reference and no regrets.
fails: {N} is out of a job by Friday, and the story follows {N} to the next interview.
fails: Nothing changes, except that {N} is now the one who made a scene.

== the body says stop
tier: life event
stages: mature
age: 40-65
holds: reckless
per_year: 0 0 0 0 .3 0
gap: 2-5
alpha: W.3 U.3 B.15 R.1 G.15
times: an estimate: about one person in three who is reckless meets it in a year of midlife, when years of running hot catch up; it comes back now and then for as long as the state holds (shadows.md)
likelier: long hours for years; little sleep; a job or a cause {N} loves too much to leave
rarer: a body used to rest; work that ends at five
tone: trouble
life: health, work
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague
earth: {N} has run on adrenaline for years, and the body is starting to refuse
scene: The chest pains came again on the stairs at work. {N} has been doing three people's jobs on four hours' sleep, and loves most minutes of it. The doctor wants tests and a month off.
scene R: Slowing down feels like a little death. {N} has always run hot, and running hot is when {N} feels most alive.
- R | skip the tests, push through the month, and rest when the work is done | v: stimulation, achievement | self_control: - | chance: 40
- W | take the month off as the doctor says, and hand the work over properly | v: conformity, security | chance: 66
- U | book the tests, read up on it, and plan a slower year | v: security, self-direction | self_control: + | chance: 66
- B | bargain for a part-time year, on the best terms you can get | v: power, security | chance: 62
- G | go and stay by the sea, walk every day, and let the body set the pace | v: security, hedonism | self_control: + | chance: 62
- W>B | keep to the doctor's rules to the letter, to come back strong on your own terms | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 62
- U>R | learn a sport that takes the same fire, and train for it properly | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 62
- B>G | sell your share of the work, and buy a quieter life near family | v: security, tradition | chance: 58
- R>W | throw all that fire into getting well, for the people who count on it | v: benevolence, stimulation | self_control: + | chance: 52
- G>U | take up something slow, a garden or a craft, and see what it teaches you | v: self-direction, tradition | self_control: + | chance: 58
works: The tests come back clear, and the slower year turns out to be a good one.
works: {N} comes back changed, still burning, but on a lower flame.
fails: The pains come back worse, and a hospital bed makes the decision for {N}.
fails: {N} pushes through, and pays for it with a winter too tired to do anything at all.

== a bridge burned years ago
tier: life event
stages: elder
age: 60-95
holds: reckless
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 .3
gap: 2-5
alpha: W.3 U.3 B.15 R.1 G.15
times: an estimate: about one person in three who is reckless meets it in a year of old age, when the people left behind start to write back; it comes back now and then for as long as the state holds (shadows.md)
likelier: an old family quarrel; a friendship ended in a single night; a funeral that brought names back
rarer: a life with no lasting quarrels
tone: mixed
life: friends, family, regret
horizon: years
roles: sibling, friend
earth: someone {N} fell out with long ago has written, and {N} has to decide whether to answer
scene: A letter came from {sibling}, after nineteen years of silence. The fight was loud and public, and {N} said things that cannot be unsaid. The letter is short and asks for nothing.
scene R: {N} has never once looked back at a burned bridge. But the hand that holds the letter is not quite steady.
- R | tear it up: what was said was meant, and it still stands | v: self-direction | chance: 40
- W | write back at once, and say you were wrong, for your part | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 66
- U | read it many times, then write a careful letter asking what changed | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 66
- B | answer politely, and find out what {sibling} wants before giving anything | v: security, power | chance: 62
- G | go and see {sibling} without writing first: family is family | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 62
- W>R | apologise properly, in person, then take {sibling} out for the meal you never had | v: benevolence, hedonism | chance: 62
- U>G | ask around the family, slowly, about {sibling}'s life before replying | v: universalism, tradition | chance: 62
- B>W | offer to settle the old money matter that started it, fairly this time | v: power, universalism | chance: 58
- R>U | ring at once, and argue it out honestly until each of you understands the other | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 52
- G>B | invite {sibling} for the holidays, and keep the past out of it, on your own terms | v: tradition, security | chance: 58
works: The first meeting is stiff, the second is easy, and {N} has a sibling again.
works: Old words are said again, differently, and this time they heal.
fails: The meeting turns into the old fight, word for word.
fails: The letter waits too long for an answer, and the next news is of a funeral.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- stuck in their ways (Green)

